<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-eldredgeops-rana-18file-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Turing k_c at 492 nm for the 18-file Eldredgeops eye (Cazenovian, 387 Ma) (Eldredgeops rana_18file)",
        "Turing k_c at 492 nm for the 18-file Eldredgeops eye (Cazenovian, 387 Ma) faithfully reproduces Eldredgeops rana_18file morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-eldredgeops-rana-18file-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-eldredgeops-rana-18file-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-eldredgeops-rana-18file-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-eldredgeops-rana-18file-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Eldredgeops rana_18file specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-eldredgeops-rana-18file-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Eldredgeops rana_18file" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: That Devonian lens pigment used these Schnakenberg coefficients.",
        "does_not_claim: That losing one lens file changes k_c.",
        "does_not_claim: That the photograph is a solution of the PDE.",
        "does_not_claim: That the unsigned nanopublications were published by the template ORCID holder.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Conserved-arc ratio 18/17 between this 387 Ma morph and the 384 Ma 17-file successor.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Fourier-split 2D nonlinear field on a 96^2 grid spanning six linear wavelengths.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: RK4 modal growth versus the 2x2 dispersion eigenvalue.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Slot parameters a=0.146, b=1.038, gamma=2.40, Du_pre=0.018, Dv_pre=0.492 rescaled so lambda_c = 492 nm.",
        "reported_in_source: Clarkson, Levi-Setti and Horváth 2006 describe schizochroal eyes as calcite lens arrays.",
        "reported_in_source: Eldredge 1972 documents Phacops (Eldredgeops) rana lens-file counts through the Middle Devonian.",
        "reported_in_source: Schnakenberg 1979 states the two-species reaction used here.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952 states the diffusion-driven instability and a critical wavenumber.",
        "transfer_boundary: 492 nm is the campaign detail-scale assignment (tier 2_macromolecular_100nm), not a length Eldredge published.",
        "transfer_boundary: The Commons photograph is an Eldredgeops rana eye, not a proven Cazenovian 18-file voucher." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Eldredgeops rana_18file (Middle Devonian (Cazenovian, 387 Ma))" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Entoma (Arthropoda)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Eldredgeops" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-eldredgeops-rana-18file-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/eldredgeops_rana_18file_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Eldredgeops rana_18file; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952 states the diffusion-driven instability and a critical wavenumber. | Schnakenberg 1979 states the two-species reaction used here. | Eldredge 1972 documents Phacops (Eldredgeops) rana lens-file counts through the Middle Devonian. | Clarkson, Levi-Setti and Horváth 2006 describe schizochroal eyes as calcite lens arrays.; reconstructed_in_script: Slot parameters a=0.146, b=1.038, gamma=2.40, Du_pre=0.018, Dv_pre=0.492 rescaled so lambda_c = 492 nm. | RK4 modal growth versus the 2x2 dispersion eigenvalue. | Fourier-split 2D nonlinear field on a 96^2 grid spanning six linear wavelengths. | Conserved-arc ratio 18/17 between this 387 Ma morph and the 384 Ma 17-file successor.; transfer_boundary: 492 nm is the campaign detail-scale assignment (tier 2_macromolecular_100nm), not a length Eldredge published. | The Commons photograph is an Eldredgeops rana eye, not a proven Cazenovian 18-file voucher.; does_not_claim: That Devonian lens pigment used these Schnakenberg coefficients. | That the photograph is a solution of the PDE. | That losing one lens file changes k_c. | That the unsigned nanopublications were published by the template ORCID holder.]; other sources: Systematics and evolution of Phacops rana (Green, 1832) and Phacops iowensis Delo, 1935 <https://digitallibrary.amnh.org/handle/2246/1095>; phenomenon_size: 357 nm (3.57e-07 m, log10=-6.447 m, tier=2_macromolecular_100nm); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 357 nm to 803 µm): 357 nm:eldredgeops-rana-17file-bioelectric-polarity, 1.1 µm:eldredgeops-rana-17file-vertex-packing, 18 µm:eldredgeops-rana-17file-turing-wavelength, 36 µm:eldredgeops-rana-17file-clock-wavefront, 80 µm:eldredgeops-rana-17file-morphogen-condensation, 98 µm:eldredgeops-rana-17file-elastic-buckling, 112 µm:eldredgeops-rana-17file-flux-canalization, 156 µm:eldredgeops-rana-17file-branching-tree" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.asd.2006.08.002>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
        <https://doi.org/10.5531/sd.paleo.7> ;
    pk:externalAtlasDataset <https://paleobiodb.org/classic/checkTaxonInfo?taxon_name=Eldredgeops>,
        <https://www.morphosource.org/Search/index?search=Eldredgeops> ;
    pk:fossilLineageGroup "Trilobite Segmentation & Eye Fossil Series" ;
    pk:geologicalAgeMa 3.87e+02 ;
    pk:geologicalPeriod "Middle Devonian (Cazenovian, 387 Ma)" ;
